{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Whose</b> — the son of Balaam said that וימינם (their right hand) is in the language of Kedar, meaning their oath. But the correct interpretation in my eyes is its plain sense, and the meaning is their strength and their might. So their mouth is falsehood and their strength is deceit — speech and deed."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 144, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:42:41.172717003Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}